      "message": "Since the actions are really RPC calls then it may make sense to simplify the interfaces as follows:\n\n1) The RPCs really refer to a list of alarms ids to suppress or enable after a suppression.   Therefore, it\u0027s better to only create the alarmid(s) messages as shown below.  These messages should be in the event.proto file, not in the device.proto.\n\nmessage AlarmID {\n     string id \u003d 1;\n}\n\nmessage AlarmIDs {\n     repeated AlarmID \u003d 1\n}\n\n2)  Instead of the \"UpdateDeviceAlarmConfigs(voltha.AlarmConfigs)\" rpc call, it\u0027s better to have these two calls:\n\n\u003e EnableAlarm(AlarmIDs) return ...\n\u003e SupressAlarm(AlarmIDs) return ...",
